/** @page avrorelnotes avro Module Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    @section avro_1_0 avro Module Version 1.0

    Initial release, shipped with %Qore 3.0.

    - Avro schema parsing from JSON text or from %Qore data, with a named-type registry supporting
      recursive and re-referenced types, aliases, and field defaults
    - binary datum encode and decode for every Avro type: \c null, \c boolean, \c int, \c long,
      \c float, \c double, \c bytes, \c string, \c record, \c enum, \c array, \c map, \c union and
      \c fixed
    - every logical type: \c decimal (converted exactly at arbitrary precision), \c uuid, \c date,
      \c time-millis, \c time-micros, \c timestamp-millis, \c timestamp-micros,
      \c local-timestamp-millis, \c local-timestamp-micros and \c duration
    - reader/writer schema resolution following the specification's reconciliation rules: field
      addition and removal, defaults, reordering, aliases, numeric promotions,
      \c string / \c bytes interchange, enum defaults and unions on either side
    - object container files with the \c null and \c deflate codecs, over a file path, a \c binary
      value, or a %Qore @ref Qore::InputStream "InputStream" / @ref Qore::OutputStream
      "OutputStream"; @ref Qore::Avro::AvroFileReader "AvroFileReader" is an
      @ref Qore::AbstractIterator "AbstractIterator"
    - Parsing Canonical Form and the CRC-64-AVRO fingerprint for content-addressed schema caches
    - the companion <a href="../../AvroUtil/html/index.html#avroutilintro">AvroUtil</a> user
      module, mapping Avro schemas to
      <a href="../../DataProvider/html/index.html#dataproviderintro">data provider</a> types
    - sandbox-aware: filesystem access is tagged with the
      @ref Qore::PO_NO_FILESYSTEM "FILESYSTEM" functional domain, and every unbounded encode and
      decode loop is a cancellation point
*/
